WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.270
Keep on holding me

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.270
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:09.150
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:09.150
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:21.960
If I reach out in the light, I can touch

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:21.960
Hikari no naka ni te wo sashinobaseba todoku

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.130
The precious arms

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.130
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.130
I have been searching for so hard

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.130
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.470
I turn around and the sky of blue

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.470
Furimukeba kodoku ni wa

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:48.940
Smiles down upon my solitude

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:48.940
Sora ga aoku hohoende kureru

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:56.200
In the darkness, I nearly lose sight of my dreams

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:56.200
Kurayami ni yume wo miushinai sou ni naru

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:04.120
But if you remain by my side

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:04.120
Demo anata ga itekureru no nara

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
Keep on holding me

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.090
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.090
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:19.260
I want to protect this love for always

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:19.260
Itsudemo kono omoi wo mamoritai no

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.600
This love...

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.600
Omoi wo

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:55.420
Kurau... Your mother's sister, Aunt Kleine, and your Uncle Frank.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.930
From now on, you'll live at your aunt's house.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.770
I told you the reason why last night, remember?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.400
I must not stay at the laboratory.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.110
That's right. Because there are people
who are after your powers.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.080
Kurau, take care.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.540
Listen to what your aunt and uncle say, okay?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.170
One day Dad will...

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.850
Dad!

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.490
Dad! Dad!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.290
Dad...

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.880
Kurau! Dad will always be thinking of you!

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.430
Yesterday, Today, Tomorrow

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:37.110
That's where you'll be living starting today, Kurau.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.440
Isn't it nice?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.110
It's your new home.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.470
What's the matter, Kurau?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.520
Nothing... This taste brings back memories.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.310
It's good. Really good.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.940
Eat up. You must be tired
from all the talking we did.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.650
I'm sorry to surprise you like this.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.910
Oh no, I'm glad you came here, Kurau.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.290
Would you like some more, Christmas?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.960
Yes, please.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.340
She looks just like you when you first came to our house.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.050
Only her hair is longer.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.470
So, Kurau... Tell me...

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.300
Why did you name her Christmas?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.010
It just came to me.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.850
It just warmed my heart.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:56.480
I see...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.530
it's a nice name, Christmas.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.820
Thank you!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.910
That's nice, isn't it, Christmas?

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:06.530
Yeah!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:21.300
Kurau told me that you're
her mother's younger sister.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.510
That's right.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.300
Did she say anything about her mother?

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.850
That she doesn't have one...

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:37.900
Flight... She died from an illness
when Kurau was still little.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.770
You understand?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:44.030
It seems Kurau doesn't remember her mother very well.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.820
She was still very young.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.830
But... I'm sure she hasn't forgotten everything about her.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.580
Sometimes, people are helped
by the memories they have.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.290
I'm sure she's like that too...

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.050
Are you sure it's okay?

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.340
If the GPO finds out that we're here,
it'll cause trouble for you.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.050
Don't worry about that.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.810
I'm more worried about your father.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.640
Yes...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.270
And I don't have any way of contacting the Agent who helped us.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.230
I'll ask an old friend I used to
work with to look into that.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.030
Looks like they've become fast friends.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.820
I think she's relieved to be here.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.410
You get some rest here too.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.040
You've been fighting all along.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.670
The ship Kurau was on was destroyed by a
stray shot exploding the weapons on board.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.840
We could not find Kurau.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.930
I know this must be very sad news for you.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.190
Are you okay, Dr. Amami?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.860
Kurau... My daughter... died a long time ago.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.490
Isn't that what I've always said?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:13.780
Doctor!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.790
Inspector Wong,

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.120
there is something that I must do.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.790
Please leave the treatment of the Ryna sapiens up to me.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.170
Dr. Amami didn't seem to believe it.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.510
Of course not!

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.090
Who would ever believe that both
Kurau and Christmas are dead?!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.680
There were no survivors. That's the truth.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.650
We have no reason to keep you here any more.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.610
You are released, former Officer Doug.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.420
Those girls are...

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.550
Where am I supposed to go now?

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.150
Hello?

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.150
Hello?

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.530
Is it you, Dad?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.700
Yeah, it's me, Teddy.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.700
Dad! How come you didn't call me
for such a long time? I... I...

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.380
Teddy... I'm sorry...

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.710
Forgive me...

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.750
Don't cry.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:57.390
Teddy... Don't cry... Please...

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.350
Yes, just like that... Knead it well.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.850
Good job!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:58.570
Hmm...

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.410
It doesn't look like anyone's searching for you.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.000
The GPO probably thinks we died in space.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.000
I wish we could at least let your father know you're alive.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.130
I feel like I've become a ghost...

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.590
I want to go look for Dad and Doug, but I can't do anything.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.520
It's not that you can't do anything.
You're alive, aren't you?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:27.560
Yes.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.400
All you can do for now is wait, Kurau.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.010
I used to stare out into the lake like this a lot.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:00.180
But since I didn't have you,
I was all alone back then.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.440
What are you writing?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:14.730
A letter...

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:21.450
I promised Dad that I wouldn't even send him a letter.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.740
So that's why this is a letter that won't be sent.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:29.460
Uncle was concerned about how sad I was.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:33.130
So he would take me hiking almost every day.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.840
Wait, Frank!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.600
You're tough, Uncle.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.610
I used to be an Agent.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.530
I had a lot of training.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.070
Agent?

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.990
Yeah, it's a job that helps people.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.240
I quit after I injured my leg.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.620
But Uncle can do anything, right?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.080
Yup!

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.420
It was fun.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.000
So much, that I almost forgot my loneliness.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.250
But one day...

00:12:58.790 --> 00:12:59.710
Frank!

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.640
Frank!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.520
Are you okay?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.440
I...

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.480
I'm sorry...

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.360
Why are you apologizing?

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.240
I was... scared...

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:31.790
Kurau.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.500
It's okay now. I'm fine.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.540
I'm sorry.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:42.710
Don't apologize. You were only trying to rescue me.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.090
B-But...

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.800
I injured Dad with my powers...

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.930
Yes, your father told me.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:58.600
But he told you it wasn't your fault, right?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.190
But...

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.860
Come on, stand up now.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.070
Okay...

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.240
Okay.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.450
Listen carefully, Kurau.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.790
You must not be scared all the time.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.590
At times, strong powers may hurt others,

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:26.090
but depending on how they're used,
they can help others, too.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.060
Help others?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:35.430
Right.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.020
I can?

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.480
Dad, I never thought of it till then.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:49.240
That my power may be useful to others...

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.240
I've been thinking about this ever since.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:58.250
Uncle Frank has been teaching me
many things to become an Agent.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.870
As long as I'm in this world,

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:05.920
I want to live standing on my own two feet,
using my own two hands.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.260
That's how I've been thinking lately.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:35.030
I still don't know anything about
this vast world I'm in.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:41.000
Dad... I'm always thinking of you.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:46.300
But... This will be my last letter that won't be sent.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.030
What a good girl, Kurau.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.400
Good girl?

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:17.990
Because you decided on your own
to become an Agent, right?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:18.660
Yeah.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.660
Do you remember how you felt back then?

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:30.800
I remember now.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.010
You want to work?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.260
Yes, any job you have here is fine.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:44.060
If there's something I can do, then I want to do it.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:50.570
I don't want to stay here with you
and not do anything every day.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.530
I understand how you feel...

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.860
But if the GPO finds out...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.910
It wouldn't be a good idea to register as an Agent.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.370
So I'll be your middle man.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.160
Really? Uncle!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:06.670
But I'm sure the jobs we get around here are pretty boring for you.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:11.000
That's okay. As long as I can do something. Thank you!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.290
Teddy!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.210
Dad!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:51.800
Teddy!

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.090
Wow, you've gotten heavy!

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.350
Teddy... I mean, Ted.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:08.060
Mom and Dad can't live together any more.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:13.320
But Dad will take some time off
from work for a while.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.990
You and I can spend a lot of time together.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.490
I'll take you to lots of places.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:19.950
Really?

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.530
Yeah, and we can talk about lots of things.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:27.960
Oh yeah, Ted. Let me tell you about this super strong Agent I met.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.590
You like people who are brave, right?

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:32.420
Yup!

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:37.840
She was brave and no matter what
happened, she wouldn't be defeated.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.180
No matter what happened...

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.690
Only those who have permission from
Headquarters are allowed to visit.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:58.820
I have permission.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:18:59.490
What?

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.370
Chief Ichise.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.540
Wh-What do you want?

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:16.250
I had a bad feeling when I heard you left the research team.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.880
I checked and found you here.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.600
Why are you a Ryna sapien?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:29.180
It was my mistake. I made a mistake
during an experiment.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.520
What kind of experiment?

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.110
It was my mistake!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.230
That's a lie.

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.860
You've been told not to talk about it. By whom?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:42.570
I don't know! I know nothing!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.420
We're going!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.880
See you later!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.800
Wait up, Kurau!

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.420
Christmas... What a wonderful girl...

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.720
She really is like Kurau's little sister.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.720
I wonder what my sister would say if she were alive...

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:09.980
Yeah, I know...

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.190
Okay, I'm off.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:22.030
Good luck on your job.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:26.120
It's been a long time since I did security for a town festival.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.950
I'm sure I'll come home starving!

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.910
Yeah! I'll cook something nice and wait for you!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.210
Everything was the same as always.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:41.010
I felt the sky and the wind were
gently watching over us.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.720
I felt nothing bad could happen.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.690
Kurau?

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:28.140
I finally... found you...

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.140
You are...

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.520
...my Pair!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.910
From a great distance

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.910
Tooku haruka kanata kara

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:56.250
You smile at me

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:56.250
Kimi ga hohoemu you ni

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:05.420
The hopelessness that lingers from the past

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:05.420
Kako kara tsuzuku hakanasa

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:14.470
Is depicted in silence

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:14.470
Shizuka ni utsushi dasarete

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:23.730
Moonlight, please never change

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:23.730
Moonlight kawarazu ni ite

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:32.830
Moonlight, I'll come to see you

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:32.830
Moonlight ai ni yuku Kimi ni

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:41.960
Moonlight, I'll come running up and surely

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:41.960
Moonlight kakenobori kitto

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:51.090
Moonlight, we'll be able to meet again

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:51.090
Moonlight mou ichido aeru

00:22:53.310 --> 00:23:00.310
Moonlight

00:22:53.310 --> 00:23:00.310
Moonlight

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.910
Next Episode

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.990
Security guard!

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:15.660
Big trouble! Big trouble! Hurry, come!

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:16.660
What's the matter?

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:18.870
This way, this way!

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:19.790
See?

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.630
Well, this certainly is a serious problem...

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.880
Anxiety Of The Swallowtail Butterfly
